# `--cycle-collector off` (plans/backlog/WEAK_AND_UNCOLLECTED_RC.md §1, W1):
# the fixture's garbage cycle is tracked and collected under the default
# `auto`, untracked and leaked under `off`, and the `--debug-heap` oracle's
# live-at-exit count is the leak's only witness under `off`. The last command
# pins the flag's validation. The test binary's output rides the runner's `-v`
# output with its build chatter, so stdout keeps only the probe line, the
# report's live-at-exit count and the error.
stdout_keep_match=(cycle: tracked [0-9]+, disposed [0-9]+|live at exit: [0-9]+ blocks|invalid --cycle-collector .*)
timeout=600
